ci: add GitHub Actions workflow for lint/typecheck/test/build

Adds .github/workflows/ci.yml so every push to a feature branch and
every PR to main / codex/base44-deploy-nick gets validated:

  1. ESLint (--quiet — errors block, warnings allowed)
  2. TypeScript (currently non-blocking — types are stale, see
     TECH_DEBT.md; flip to blocking once supabase types are
     regenerated)
  3. Vitest (480 tests passing today)
  4. Production Vite build

Concurrency group cancels redundant runs on the same branch when
new commits arrive, so rapid iteration doesn't pile up CI runs.

Pre-flight cleanup so the workflow is green on first run:
  - Auto-fixed 12 unused-import errors via `npm run lint:fix`.
    Files affected: ScheduleCascadeReason.jsx, RFIDetailModal.jsx,
    RoundTimeline.jsx, DrawingSubmittalHub.jsx, ProjectsHealth.jsx,
    TeamDashboard.jsx, Timeline.jsx, UnbilledRevenue.jsx.
  - Removed a dead `eslint-disable-next-line import/no-unresolved`
    in Tutorial.jsx — the rule isn't loaded in our eslint config.
    The disable was unnecessary; the import works at build time
    via Vite's `?raw` query.

Also adds TECH_DEBT.md as the running list of known issues, with
each entry carrying:
  - Where (path)
  - What (description)
  - Impact (severity / surface area)
  - Fix (concrete remediation path)

This is the "tech debt markdown" item from the user's enterprise-
readiness roadmap. The next contributor (or future me) can scan it
in 60 seconds and know what's still on the list.

